A||||9||RFMike||Fiero high speed frontal impact||||1||
Z||000000||RFMike||04-02-2000||12:07 AM||||After many e-mails to the NHTSA, I finally got a copy of the crash test tabulations for the Fiero, and many other vehicles.  It is in  Microsoft Excel format, for those of you interested, I could e-mail you a copy, but you have to have Excel, or a compatible.<BR>This is part of a message:<P> "We tested an 84 Fiero in the frontal impact.  It received a 5 star rating for both the passenger and driver.  The vehicle was not side impacted.  Side impact testing was not conducted at that time."<P>So much for the comments I have heard that claimed that the Fiero was rated 5 star for front, side, and rear impact.  <BR>There were no cars that received those ratings in 1984, since they did not test for those collisions at that time.  It is true, however, that it is remarkably crash resistant.  In reviewing the data, one column indicates deformation, and the Fiero had 5%, which was the lowest of all the cars listed.  I am assuming that this is compartment deformation.<BR>The spread sheet has several columns that do not mean anything to me, and I think the NHTSA people are sick of me!  If anyone knows what the various headings are, I would be interested in feedback.<P>TIA,<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-02-2000||01:01 AM||||Mike,<P>To the best of my knowledge what you have is correct from NHTSA. Please e-mail me those results.<P>Keep in mind NHTSA tests are full frontal tests. NHTSA does not do the offset test that IIHS does. (This may have changed recently, but I don't believe so.)Results of that test are often far diferant than NHTSA's testing. Many 5 star NHTSA cars have failed that test completely. I expect Fiero would do good in that test as well tho after seing some of the wrecks I've seen. I don't know if the IIHS ever tested a Fiero the data doesn't go back very far online.<P><A HREF="http://www.hwysafety.org/default.htm" TARGET=_blank>Insurance Institute for Highway Safety, Highway Loss Data Institute</A>||||reg||1
