Z||000007||RFMike||04-02-2000||09:20 AM||||Ogre,<BR>IIHS doesn't carry data for our cars, as far as I could determine.  I e-mailed them several times, and couldn't get a response.<P>For anyone looking at this info, keep in mind that the test is based on crashing the car into a stationary barrier.  This is similar to a single car crash.  If another, heavier vehicle smacks you, the dynamics are completely different, as that vehicle has it's own kinetic energy;  that's why it isn't good to get t-boned by a Suburban going 55.<P>I also think the car would fare well in side and rear crashes, given what I've seen in salvage yards.  The driver/ passenger compartment is rarely trashed, even with major body damage.<BR>||||reg||1
